# Financial data

- Keep `observed_at` distinct from `retrieved_at`.
- Never coerce a missing value to zero.
- Do not use a stale close as the current reference price.
- Do not average conflicting observations.
- Apply vacancy only when a FII is classified as brick.
- Label scenario shocks as assumptions. Do not call them probabilities.
- Truncate price series at `as_of` before any calculation.
- A named investor pattern may only restate an emitted metric. Do not add intrinsic value, a ceiling price, a dividend hurdle, a moat score, or a crypto price model.
